  "query_preview": "../Monday through Thursday/...We are back in an active\npattern here in Southeast, with a new low and frontal system on \nthe docket every few days. To start the workweek a shortwave will \nmove north through the southern and to a lesser extent, central \npanhandle. While lighter rain will continue throughout, periods of\nheavier rain are possible with this wave. Then come Wednesday, \nanother Gulf low will intensify in the western Gulf, meanwhile a \nfront attendant to that low will swipe north and bring the next \nserious bout of rain to the entirety of the panhandle. Towards the\nend of the week a quickly deepening low will move quickly from \nthe south into the Gulf. Deterministic guidance is in disagreement\nof the final track, but most of them have the central pressure \nreaching between 960-970 mb. The track and intensity should be \ntaken with a grain of salt at this point in the forecast process \nthough.",
